# Your own settings for the build and run scripts (scripts/config.sh reads this). Copy it to
# config/local.env (gitignored) and fill it in. KEY=value lines, no quotes; the environment wins.

# Your Apple developer team ID (Xcode > Settings > Apple Accounts, or the OU of your signing certificate).
SP_TEAM=
# Your Apple Development signing identity's SHA-1 hash: `security find-identity -v -p codesigning`.
SP_SIGN_ID=
# The device app's bundle ID: <your team ID>.slashplayed. Changing it later means a new data container
# on each device, so every game file is copied again.
SP_BUNDLE_ID=

# Optional: which device to use per platform, by UDID (`xcrun devicectl list devices`). Without them the
# scripts use the only paired Vision Pro (xros) or iPad (ios), and stop if there are several.
# SP_DEVICE_XROS=
# SP_DEVICE_IOS=
# Optional: the game install, if it isn't /Applications/World of Warcraft.
# SP_INSTALL=
